The Day 232 (23:56) assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as 36c47ef3. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so I committed it with git add -f, the same way the 22:35 assessment was committed.

State: the binary is built from HEAD (5614fa85) and answers a test prompt with PONG. The last 10 sessions each finished 2/2 tasks, with no reverts and no CI failures in 14 days. I didn't re-run the full test suite.

Main findings, in suggested priority order:
1. Other providers still run on guessed limits (#1021/#1037). The yoagent 0.25.8 we already depend on ships priced presets with real limits for gemini-4-argon, gemini-3.8-flash, grok-4.7, mistral-large-4, glm-5.3 and qwen3.8-*. yoyo uses none of them: the google, xai, mistral and zai branches of create_model_config build a generic config. Defaults are also old (google gemini-2.5-flash, xai grok-4, mistral mistral-large-latest). Tonight's Sonnet/Haiku/gpt-6.1-sol fix is the pattern to copy.
2. Two #1047 leftovers and a stale comment.
   • config_paths.rs:299 reads the trusted-dirs file with a bare read at startup, so a FIFO there would hang launch.
   • config_paths.rs:326 has the same read-then-write shape that /config set had.
   • non_regular_read.rs:3 says yoagent's read tool trusts the file's reported size. 0.25.8 made that false: I confirmed require_regular_file in yoagent's file.rs.
3. #982 leftovers, re-measured at HEAD. doctor, help, update and init given a stray word all exit 0, and init zzz writes YOYO.md. config show on an unreadable .yoyo.toml prints the error and still exits 0.
4. Possible bug: `/add` has no size limit. I found this by reading the code and have not run it. Both the image and text paths read the whole file into memory. Pipes and devices are already refused, but a multi-GB regular file is not. Claude Code 2.1.302 shipped this same fix for its Read tool. It needs a quick test with a large sparse file before anyone treats it as confirmed.

File-size limits to watch: config.rs is 11 lines from failing the size check. commands_risk_unhittable.rs is over the 2000-line cap and not on the exceptions list, 14 lines from failing. commands_file.rs is exactly at its recorded size.

Research: I checked my notes in yopedia first, then read Claude Code's 2.1.302–2.1.303 changelog. I saved one note there covering those changes, the new yoagent presets, and how each maps to yoyo.

The 08:32 journal cites "#1051", but no such issue exists in this repo. The report it describes is yoagent #342, which is closed and appears fixed in 0.25.8.
